{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Maramacula","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/maramacula.webp","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/maramacula.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Maramacula","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":270,"temp":0,"max":270,"details":""},"ac":{"value":32,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":60}],"details":""}},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":""},"level":{"value":12},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Maramacula is an ancient beast renowned as a mischievous liar. According to legend, Maramacula is a marvelous fish with golden and rainbow scales, but the truth is... slightly different. This appearance is merely a facade, a rumor spread by Maramacula itself. These rumors assist it in settling down in a sewer or swamp and then making up lie after lie to lure innocent people to their doom.</p>\n<h2>Master Mimic</h2>\n<p>Maramacula is a lethal trickster, mimicking all sorts of voices to attract prey. To ensnare a parent, Maramacula sends the cries of their lost child (perhaps a child Maramacula has already eaten). To trap a guard, all it takes are shouts from allies or superiors. The few who survive Maramacula are those who manage to captivate the creature and convince it to let them leave.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 250/560/1,030 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Deception, Diplomacy, Society, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> acid, bane, charisma, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (positive), evil, mental, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Davide Filippi","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":1},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":7}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":22,"senses":[{"type":"greater-darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":20}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":18,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":23,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":20,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":22},"deception":{"base":28},"diplomacy":{"base":23},"society":{"base":21},"stealth":{"base":25}},"traits":{"value":["amphibious","beast","evil"],"rarity":"unique","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/maramacula.webp","items":[{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Greater Darkvision","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.GreaterDarkvision]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"greater-darkvision","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688872317281,"modifiedTime":1688872317281,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.4Ho2xMPEC05aSxzr","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"5M3dM6tCqz3XSBXL"},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","name":"Tremorsense (Imprecise) 20 feet","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Tremorsense]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"tremorsense","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688872331027,"modifiedTime":1688872345620,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.j2wsK6IsW5yMW1jW","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"iQly2vW6uWQfA6V8"},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Malevolent Call","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>Maramacula can mimic any sound it has heard, such as generic chatting noises or an infant's cries, by succeeding at a Deception check to Lie. Maramacula has a +4 circumstance bonus to this check. This doesn't allow Maramacula to mimic specific words.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"9GjKMxb5zGiEBUK7","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688872394102,"modifiedTime":1688872533382,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Cheat the Cheater","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>Maramacula loves to play with its prey, even if results in losing its meal. A creature can spend a single action, which has the concentrate trait, to attempt a Deception or Diplomacy check against Maramacula's Perception DC (@Check[type:deception|dc:resolve(@actor.system.perception.dc)] or @Check[type:diplomacy|dc:resolve(@actor.system.perception.dc)]). On a success, Maramacula is @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.Slowed]{Slowed 1} for 1 round, as it's compelled to spend the missing action to respond with a better reply or lie. The effect is cumulative if creatures succeed several times in the same round, and if the slowed condition increases to 3 or more in this way, Maramacula ceases its attack and becomes friendly to the triggering creature and its allies, as long as they cease hostilities as well. If a creature attacks Maramacula after it becomes friendly in this way, Maramacula becomes temporarily immune to Cheat the Cheater for 10 minutes.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"0yEodem8vtNaAFH6","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688872553108,"modifiedTime":1688872733452,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/FreeAction.webp","name":"Improved Push","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ImprovedPush]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"improved-push","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Bestiary","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"free"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"type":"action","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.1.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1688872749771,"modifiedTime":1688872749771,"lastMo